      en: "Rio Contador is a wild mountain river in northwestern São Tomé, crashing through spectacular gorges into the sea. Its water is crystal-clear and ice-cold, originating directly from the highland rainforests. The river is known for its natural power, which was used in the past to operate one of the island's first hydroelectric plants, whose ruins are now being reclaimed by nature."
