      en: "Rio Manuel Jorge is a lively river on the east coast of São Tomé, flowing through fertile plantation areas and dense forest. It is known for its numerous rapids and picturesque waterfalls that pour into deep natural pools. The river plays a central role in the lives of local communities, both as a water source and as a place of recreation and spiritual significance."
