      en: "Rio Lembá is the most significant river in the west of the island, a symbol of nature's untamed power. It originates in the high peaks of the central massif and carves its way through some of São Tomé's steepest and most inaccessible valleys. Its water feeds the lush vegetation of the west, creating an environment where wilderness still rules absolutely and unchallenged."
